The '''Twinned Bottles''' is an ancient [[Spells|spell]] and [[contraption]] that evenly splits the contents of two separate vessels, regardless of distance. 

==Description==
[[File:Twinned Bottles' Seal.png|thumb|left|<small>The Casting Seal for the Twinned Bottles spell.</small>]] The Casting Seal for this contraption cannot be deciphered, as the names and functions of the [[Signs|signs]] and/or [[Sigils|sigils]] have been lost to time. It is inscribed upon two, small medallions which are then placed inside of two separate bottles. The spell allows for the contents of the two vessels to remain evenly split, no matter the distance between them. The spell activates as liquid runs along the shallow etchings of the seals.{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}}{{Ref|''Witch Hat Atelier'' [[Volume 12]] Extra Page: The Seals and Contraptions of Witch Hat}}
